<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia nominates IMF executive director.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia nominates IMF executive director.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia on Tuesday nominated senior public servant Greg Taylor as an executive director for the International Monetary Fund.</p>
<p>The fund has 24 executive directors, most of them representing a constituency of several countries.</p>
<p>Taylor will represent South Korea, Australia, New Zealand, Mongolia, Papua New Guinea and several Pacific and Indian Ocean island states, Treasure Peter Costello said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
